// NodeService: how a node joins a panel and how the two talk for the rest of its life.
//
// One thing decides the shape of everything here. The panel has no public IP - it sits
// behind a tunnel - so it can never dial a node. The node is always the gRPC client and
// the panel is always the server, and every "the panel tells the node to..." below is a
// message travelling down the response side of a stream the node opened (design
// section 5.2). The second thing is that such a stream drops, routinely: nothing here
// carries a delta, so reconnecting means resending the whole spec and it does not
// matter how long the node was gone.
//
// Authentication is in gRPC metadata, and this is the only place it is written down:
//
//   wisper-node-id       the node id from EnrollResponse
//   wisper-node-token    the long-lived credential from EnrollResponse
//   wisper-protocol      the protocol version in decimal, so the panel can refuse an
//                        incompatible node before it has parsed a frame
//
// Enroll is the one RPC carrying none of them: there is no credential yet, and it
// authenticates with the single-use bootstrap token in its body.
//
// Over 300 lines and not split further because it is one conversation - handshake,
// commands, acknowledgements and status all reference each other. The parts with their
// own vocabulary (the spec, terminals, files, stats, backups, databases, builds) are
// already their own files, and this one only references them.

